To fix the 403 Forbidden errors and improve the image importing:

1.  **Fixing the Preview (403 Error):** The "403 Forbidden" error in the app preview often happens because the browser sends a "Referrer" header that tells the image server "I am requesting this from your-app-domain.com", and the server blocks it (Hotlink Protection). I will add `referrerPolicy="no-referrer"` to the image preview, which mimics a direct browser visit and often bypasses this block.
2.  **Stopping URL Corruption:** I will remove the "Smart Upscaling" logic (rewriting URLs) in the excel service. While well-intentioned, modifying URL parameters often breaks the digital signature of the image, causing the server to reject it (403). I will instead rely entirely on the AI to find the correct high-res URL originally.
3.  **Prompt Refinement:** I will update the prompt to specifically ask for "Publicly Accessible" URLs.

